/-!
# The image of an integral closed subscheme under the map of Stacks 0FEW

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project and let `i : X ⟶ Y` be a
closed immersion of schemes locally of finite type over `S`, with `Y` regular and quasi-compact.
Proposition 0FEW concerns the composition

  `K'₀(X) ⟶ K₀(D_{X,perf}(𝒪_Y)) ⟶ A^*(X ⟶ Y) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`,   `[ℱ] ↦ ch(X ⟶ Y, ℱ[0]) ∩ [Y]`,

and its proof reduces the proposition to two conditions. The first, that a coherent module
supported in `δ`-dimension `≤ k` goes into degrees `≤ k`, is
`Stacks.Chow.isDimensionTriangular_coherentChowCharacter`. This file proves the second, in the
form in which the source's argument gives it: for an integral closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X` of
`δ`-dimension `k`, the image of `[𝒪_Z]` is `[Z]` plus a rational combination of classes of
integral closed subschemes of `Z` other than `Z`.

The argument is the source's. By Stacks 0FB7, `ch(X ⟶ Y, 𝒪_Z[0]) = (Z ⟶ X)_* ∘ ch(Z ⟶ Y, 𝒪_Z[0])`,
so the image of `[𝒪_Z]` is the pushforward of `ch(Z ⟶ Y, 𝒪_Z[0]) ∩ [Y] ∈ CH_*(Z) ⊗ 𝐐`.

* In degrees `j ≠ k` this class lives in `CH_j(Z) ⊗ 𝐐` with `j < k`, which is spanned by the
  classes of the integral closed subschemes of `Z` of `δ`-dimension `j`; these are other than `Z`.
* In degree `k`, since `CH_k(Z) = 𝐙 [Z]`, the class may be computed over an open neighbourhood `V`
  of the generic point `ξ` of `Z` in `Y`. The maximal ideal of the regular local ring `𝒪_{Y, ξ}`
  is generated by a regular sequence (Stacks 00NQ), so `V` may be chosen with `Z ∩ V ⟶ V` cut out
  by a regular sequence (Stacks 063I), and Lemma 0FEH, the consequence of Lemma 0FEG on the
  fundamental class, gives `[Z ∩ V]`.

The conditions then give the conclusions of Proposition 0FEW for this composition: the
surjectivity of `K'₀(X) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, the bijectivity of the canonical maps
`CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ gr_k K'₀(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, and the reduction of injectivity to the separation of the
filtration by dimension of supports. Injectivity itself, and Proposition 0FEW, are in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.RationalIntersection.ChowCoherentIsomorphism`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.capFundamentalClassAt_bivariantProperPushforward` — `(f_* ∘ c) ∩ [Y]_n` is
  `f_*(c ∩ [Y]_n)`.
* `Stacks.Chow.of_lTensor_properChowPushforward_mem_span` — a class pushed forward from a closed
  subscheme is a combination of classes of its integral closed subschemes.
* `Stacks.Chow.HasLeadingTermOnIntegral.isDiagonalOnIntegral` — the leading-term form of the
  conditions gives condition (2).
* `Stacks.Chow.coherentChowCharacter_mk_apply_eq_lTensor` — the degree `j` part of the image of
  `[ℱ]` as the pushforward of that of `ch(Z ⟶ Y, ℱ[0]) ∩ [Y]`.
* `Stacks.Chow.hasLeadingTermOnIntegral_coherentChowCharacter` — condition (2), in the
  leading-term form, for the composition of Stacks 0FEW.
* `Stacks.Chow.surjective_liftBaseChange_coherentChowCharacter` — `K'₀(X) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` is
  surjective.
* `Stacks.Chow.bijective_rTensor_chowToGradedCoherentKZero_of_isClosedImmersion` — the canonical
  maps `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ gr_k K'₀(X) ⊗ 𝐐` are bijective.
* `Stacks.Chow.injective_liftBaseChange_coherentChowCharacter_of_separated` — injectivity reduces
  to the separation of the filtration by dimension of supports.

## Implementation notes

The conclusion of Lemma 0FEG for the structure sheaf of every regular closed immersion of
positive codimension into a quasi-compact scheme locally of finite type over `S` is
`Stacks.Chow.isRegularImmersionChernFormula_of_compactSpace`
(LocalizedChern/RegularImmersionChernFormula.lean).

The integral closed subscheme `Z = Z_x` of `X` through a point `x` is presented, for the
computation, by the integral closed subscheme `Z_{i(x)}` of `Y` through `i(x)`, which is
isomorphic to it over `X` and carries `𝒪_Z[0]` as an object of `D_{Z_{i(x)},perf}(𝒪_Y)`. The degree
`k` part is computed in `CH_k(Z) ⊗ 𝐐` and only then pushed forward to `X`, as in the source:
`CH_k(Z ∩ V) ⟶ CH_k(V)` need not be injective.

Of Stacks 0FEW, surjectivity and the "moreover" are proved here unconditionally, while
injectivity is proved only when `δ_{X/S}` is bounded below.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEW)
